Subject: [PATCH] ppu headers: ILP32-clean syscall pointer casts, missing stdint

Each of these headers fails a standalone -Wall -Wextra -Werror compile on
the PPU, which every user of them inherits:

- sys/file.h, sys/interrupt.h, sys/tty.h cast pointer arguments straight
  to u64.  Under ILP32 that is a pointer-to-integer cast of a different
  size (-Wpointer-to-int-cast).  Cast through uintptr_t first, as the
  rest of the SDK's lv2 wrappers do.  The value is unchanged: the target
  extends pointers unsigned (POINTERS_EXTEND_UNSIGNED 1), which is what
  the uintptr_t step spells out.
- sys/usbd.h passed pointers to the syscall register variables with no
  cast at all (-Wint-conversion in C, an error in C++), and two wrappers
  passed an undeclared `unk1` where their deviceNumber parameter was
  meant, so the header could not be included.
- mars/base.h cast to `const uintptr_t`; a qualifier on a cast result is
  ignored (-Wignored-qualifiers in C++).
- ssl/ssl.h used uint32_t and friends without including <stdint.h>.

No declaration, type or layout changes.

diff --git a/common/libspumars/include/ppu/mars/base.h b/common/libspumars/include/ppu/mars/base.h
index 2084060..b37d7aa 100644
--- a/common/libspumars/include/ppu/mars/base.h
+++ b/common/libspumars/include/ppu/mars/base.h
@@ -240,7 +240,7 @@ static inline void *mars_ea_to_ptr(uint64_t ea)
  */
 static inline uint64_t mars_ptr_to_ea(const void *ptr)
 {
-	return (uint64_t)(const uintptr_t)ptr;
+	return (uint64_t)(uintptr_t)ptr;
 }
 
 /**
diff --git a/ppu/include/ssl/ssl.h b/ppu/include/ssl/ssl.h
index d4d8084..9bb824b 100644
--- a/ppu/include/ssl/ssl.h
+++ b/ppu/include/ssl/ssl.h
@@ -1,6 +1,8 @@
 #ifndef __SSL_H__
 #define __SSL_H__
 
+#include <stdint.h>
+
 
 #define SSL_CIPHER_UNKNOWN                         (-1)
 #define SSL_CIPHER_RSA_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA       (0)
diff --git a/ppu/include/sys/file.h b/ppu/include/sys/file.h
index e88fa8f..5065f99 100644
